atio":0.82,"watchRatio":0.489},{"ratio":0.83,"watchRatio":0.4866},{"ratio":0.84,"watchRatio":0.48450000000000004},{"ratio":0.85,"watchRatio":0.4818},{"ratio":0.86,"watchRatio":0.48},{"ratio":0.87,"watchRatio":0.47450000000000003},{"ratio":0.88,"watchRatio":0.4693},{"ratio":0.89,"watchRatio":0.4661},{"ratio":0.9,"watchRatio":0.4646},{"ratio":0.91,"watchRatio":0.4585},{"ratio":0.92,"watchRatio":0.4531},{"ratio":0.93,"watchRatio":0.44799999999999995},{"ratio":0.94,"watchRatio":0.4456},{"ratio":0.95,"watchRatio":0.4391},{"ratio":0.96,"watchRatio":0.4325},{"ratio":0.97,"watchRatio":0.4233},{"ratio":0.98,"watchRatio":0.41100000000000003},{"ratio":0.99,"watchRatio":0.3969},{"ratio":1,"watchRatio":0.3908}],"script":{"source_path":"all-146-tagged.json","words":165,"wpm":null,"lang":"en","chapters":[],"blocks":[],"text":"Durand was amazing, but do you know the man who built an entire Indian spy agency? That man was R.N. Kao, the legendary first chief of India's foreign intelligence agency, RAW. And his elite team, they were famously called the Cowboys. Kao knew that modern espionage needed more than just police officers. So, he went straight to the universities, handpicking young, brilliant minds to build a diverse, unstoppable force. He was absolute perfectionist. Officers had to weigh every single word in their reports. If your file came back with a tick and the word off, you were spending the whole night panicking over the details that you missed. But, it wasn't strict business. To build an unbreakable brotherhood, he created the Club 71. Once a month, Kao and his wife, Malini, threw in a grand party, making the youngest, newest recruit work as bartenders just to help them break the ice and join the family. This legendary team played a crucial role in splitting Pakistan."}}